nodes.body:
> Thanks for the PR! A DSv4 run would be great but since `k = 1024` is already covered by the GPU test and the sentinel sweep, which is the v4 top-k this skip uses, I think it looks good

@frida-andersson  Thanks! One nit on the k: DeepSeek-V4-Flash's index_topk is 512 (its config.json), the same as V4.1; 1024 is V4-Pro's. Both are covered. The new mixed/padded op test runs k = 32 / 512 / 1024, and the sentinel sweep checks top_k_per_row_decode at k = 512 and 1024 on every gfx950 path below 128 rows.

V4-Flash does reach this op on MI355X by default since #63669 (AITER on and indexer dtype auto give MXFP4).

